In case you missed it, last week a team of dedicated fans was formed 
with the sole purpose of producing a new guidebook.  The current 
Guidebook is a great document (and certainly a piece of NetHack "lore" 
that has served its purpose) but it does not address some of the basic 
needs of new players:  clarity, organization, consistency and accuracy.

This, the first of our weekly status updates to RGRN, is a snapshot of 
our current progress and a reminder that we're still open to new ideas, 
suggestions and feedback.

TEAM

Currently we have seven members, including an experienced editor.  We 
have agreed that this is a good "working size", so we're not actively 
looking to increase our numbers at this stage.  That could change in the 
future.


COMMUNICATIONS WITH OFFICIAL DEVTEAM

We've had limited but encouraging email contact with the official 
DevTeam and are currently putting together a high-level proposal for 
their review.  That proposal will be submitted by the end of this 
current week.


PROGRESS TO DATE

At this stage we have:

- set up a message board and established overall team process
- started to formally track outstanding issues and discussion points
- produced an HTML proof-of-concept that we will continue to improve and 
refine until it's launch-ready.


OPEN CALL FOR FEEDBACK

I'd like to encourage everyone to respond to this thread with your 
ideas, criticisms and suggestions regarding the existing Guidebook. 
What do you think the new guidebook should include?  What shouldn't it 
include?

ALL ideas will be tabled and addressed - this is your opportunity to 
have a say and contribute to a fantastic game that has given so much to 
all of us.

Alternatively, if you have any private concerns or comments then please 
